      "section": "164",
      "quote": "Any confession or statement made to a police officer shall be recorded in the presence of a magistrate, who shall ensure that it is made voluntarily, without any inducement, threat, promise or fraud, and shall be reduced to writing, signed by the person making it, and entered in the court‑record."
    },
