      "section": "165",
      "quote": "The magistrate may, if he thinks it necessary, order a medical examination of the accused before a confession is recorded, to ascertain his physical and mental condition."
    },
    {
      "section": "166",
      "quote": "The magistrate shall read the confession to the accused, ask whether he understands it, and whether he wishes to amend or withdraw it, before signing and entering it in the register."
